after the Memorial Day ceremony,

00:48:50.450 --> 00:48:56.491
There is the cocktail and traditional reception where the Marines come to the Bulldog fountain.

00:48:57.551 --> 00:49:05.694
General Conway led me to the side of the fountain and then gave a short speech in which he recounted what I had done for the corps.

00:49:06.874 --> 00:49:08.915
And the commander took a small red box out of his pocket.

00:49:08.916 --> 00:49:09.475
a small jewel box.

00:49:10.931 --> 00:49:19.715
And so, from the screen, he produced a gold Marine Corps badge, which he then pinned to my jacket, introducing me as follows.

00:49:20.095 --> 00:49:21.195
Honorary Marines

00:49:21.255 --> 00:49:25.737
He was an honorary lifetime member of the Marine Corps and presented me with the diploma.

00:49:25.738 --> 00:49:30.459
the certificate signed by the corps commander in Washington on May 25, 2008.

00:49:32.358 --> 00:49:34.859
I raised my fist next to the commander and shouted "Hurrah!"

00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:38.441
And the entire assembly began to shout "Hurrah!"

00:49:38.961 --> 00:49:40.182
And the corps commander as well.

00:49:41.002 --> 00:49:42.823
And then I went home with that famous diploma.

00:49:43.804 --> 00:49:45.545
And that's when, upon discovering it on the internet,

00:49:45.605 --> 00:49:46.925
It was a very rare title.

00:49:46.965 --> 00:49:48.286
It was awarded to very few people.

00:49:48.986 --> 00:49:51.247
We were only two foreigners who had obtained it.

00:49:52.028 --> 00:49:52.928
Me and a Japanese man.

00:49:54.829 --> 00:49:55.690
I didn't deserve any of this.

00:49:57.090 --> 00:49:57.610
I did that.

00:49:57.630 --> 00:49:58.231
It's my passion.

00:49:58.351 --> 00:49:59.432
It's huge that he recognized him.

00:49:59.512 --> 00:50:00.312
I am very touched.

00:50:00.753 --> 00:50:01.013
But anyway,

00:50:01.033 --> 00:50:02.974
I didn't do it to get a scientific apology.

00:50:03.394 --> 00:50:06.016
and now I was part of the United States Marine Corps family.

